        // The general rule: If the transferOwnership call returned (ok == true), then c.owner() equals the provided candidateNewOwner.
        // The mutant that sets owner = address(0) will violate this for any candidateNewOwner != address(0).
        // Single assertion reading c's public getter:
        if (ok) {
            assertTrue(c.owner() == candidateNewOwner);
        } else {
            // If the call reverted, we assert nothing about owner; to keep exactly one assertTrue as required,
            // we assert the tautology that ok == false implies ok == false by asserting ok == false.
            // But the rules require exactly one assertTrue that the reference satisfies for ALL admissible inputs
